# GitHub
Anyone on GitHub, a person or an organization, and any repository, found by what you type.
Every thing it shows is in GitHub.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
A page in a browser holds no key:  it may search 10 times a minute, so the field waits for you to stop typing.

<spell-thing "github page">
	<spell>
		- its "search" is text
		- its "showing" is a user
		- to create it:
			set its search to "solid"
	</spell>

	<action "try (words as text)">
		set its showing to nothing
		set its search to words
	</action>

	<draw>
		<form value={it}>
			<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="center" justify="between">
				<header size="large">People and code, on GitHub</header>
				<ui-search name="search" parameter="s" icon="search" placeholder="A person, an organization, a repository" aria-label="Search GitHub" />
			</stack>
			<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="center" spacing="xs">
				<text size="small" color="grey">Try</text>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "ryansolid"}>ryansolid</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "solidjs"}>solidjs</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "vite"}>vite</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "torvalds"}>torvalds</button>
				<button size="small" appearance="basic pill" onClick={try "spreadsheet"}>spreadsheet</button>
			</stack>
		</form>
		<if its showing>
			<button appearance="basic" icon="arrow left" onClick={set its showing to nothing}>Back</button>
			draw the page of (the user whose id is the login of its showing)
			while waiting:
				<loader visible inline text>Asking GitHub</loader>
			if that fails:
				<text>GitHub can't find that login just now.</text>
		<otherwise>
			<header size="medium">People and organizations</header>
			<for every user matching its search as="cards" columns="6" doubling paging="pages" loading="Asking GitHub" failed="GitHub can't be searched just now:  it takes 10 searches a minute." empty="Nobody on GitHub goes by that." />
			<header size="medium">Repositories</header>
			<for every repository matching its search as="cards" columns="3" doubling paging="pages" loading="Asking GitHub" failed="GitHub can't be searched just now:  it takes 10 searches a minute." empty="No repository matches that." />
		</>
		<text size="small">
			From <link link="https://docs.github.com/en/rest">GitHub's REST API</link>, asked for as you look.
		</text>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# Someone on GitHub
A person or an organization:  a card in a search, and a page of their own, with their bio and their most popular repositories.
A search gives only a little of each:  their page reads them whole, by their login.

<spell-more-of "user">
	<draw>
		<ui-card onClick={look at it}>
			<image src={its avatar url} alt="" />
			<content>
				<header>
					{its login} <link link={its html url} target="_blank" aria-label="On GitHub"><icon name="github" /></link>
				</header>
				<meta>{its kind}</meta>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>

	<draw "page">
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="start">
			<image src={its avatar url} alt="" size="small" appearance="rounded" />
			<stack>
				<header size="large">
					{its name} <link link={its html url} target="_blank" aria-label="On GitHub"><icon name="github" /></link>
				</header>
				<text color="grey">{its login} · {its kind}</text>
				<text>{its bio}</text>
				<text size="small" color="grey">{its public repos} public repositories · {its followers} followers</text>
			</stack>
		</stack>
		<header size="medium">Most popular</header>
		<for every repository matching ("user:" + its login + " sort:stars") as="cards" columns="3" doubling paging="pages" loading="Asking GitHub" failed="GitHub can't be searched just now:  it takes 10 searches a minute." empty="Nothing public yet." />
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# A repository
Its name, what it's for, and how many people starred it;  its GitHub icon opens it on GitHub, in a new window.

<spell-more-of "repository">
	<draw>
		<ui-card>
			<content>
				<header>
					{its full name} <link link={its html url} target="_blank" aria-label="On GitHub"><icon name="github" /></link>
				</header>
				<meta>★ {its stargazers count} · {its language}</meta>
				<description>{its description}</description>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>


# What someone on GitHub can do, from anywhere
Shown on their own page, in the GitHub tab of the public servers.

<spell>
	to look at (a user):
		set the showing of the github of the public servers to it
</spell>
